      "content": "To address the inconsistent ink transfer, I recommend checking the heat press temperature and time settings. For polyester blends, a lower temperature may be ideal, perhaps around 280-300°F (138-149°C), which can help prevent overheating and distortions. Additionally, ensuring consistent pressure and adhering to the recommended pressure distribution (e.g., even pressure on the entire press) will also help to optimize the ink transfer.",
