    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. we checked the temp and it seems steady, and the pressure plates are clean and even. we even tried a new batch of paper. the weird thing is, it's not even a consistent failure. we'll have 10 shirts look perfect, and then the 11th one just has these random faded spots where the color just seems to have missed the fabric entirely. it's almost like the ink isn't sticking right even though the settings are correct. any idea why it would be so random like that?",
