      "role": "user",
      "content": "we've checked the fabric for lint and finishes and it's a clean batch. we even ran a test on a bare piece of the fabric without any print and it still seems to have these microscopic thin spots where the dye won't take. it's really frustrating because the settings are perfect and the materials are clean, but the ink just... vanishes in certain sections of the press. is there anything else that could cause the ink to just fail to transfer like that?",
